      "rationale": "L1 explicitly names position 97 for KCNJ15, and L2 provides the flanking sequence GDLEP(97)-[PGG-HA-PGG]-(98)EPIS, unambiguously placing the junction after P97 and before G98. Python verification confirms seq[96]='P' and seq[97]='G', matching the paper exactly. Position 97 lies 6 residues from the TM1 C-terminal boundary (residue 91) and 46 residues from TM2 (residue 143), well within the extracellular loop (residues 92\u2013142). The two extracellular cysteines (C107, C139) are 10 and 42 residues downstream, so the insertion does not directly disrupt the putative disulfide pair. HA epitope tag inserted into the extracellular loop of full-length KCNJ15 after residue 97 (P97), flanked by PGG linkers on both sides (creating ...GDLEP[97]-PGG-YPYDVPDYA-PGG-[98]EPIS...), expressed as cRNA in Xenopus laevis oocytes. Surface expression measured by luminescence assay two days post-injection.",
