  "literature_notes": "Only one extracellular loop exists in KCNJ15 (residues 92\u2013142, between TM1 and TM2). L1 and L2 together pin the validated junction to after P97. L3 corroborates surface expression but its verbatim quote names KCNJ10/KCNJ16 rather than KCNJ15; it was used only as supporting context and not as the primary grounding clip. No other ledger lines support additional sites. The N-glycosylation sequon N103-H-T (NHT) is 6 residues downstream of the insertion; the paper's successful surface display suggests the tag does not abolish trafficking, but proximity to this sequon should be noted. C107 and C139 likely form a conserved Kir disulfide; the insertion at 97 is upstream of both and was tolerated in the published construct.",
